      "writtenOn": "2025-10-17T10:07:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I know we need this, but it makes me nervous from a security perspective.\n\nI see your point. It is basically a new potential attack vector. I\u0027m nervous as well.\n\n\u003e Can we design some sort of authentication mechanism or something along those lines?\n\nDo you have anything special in your mind? You mean something like integrity check via some magic number, not to accidentally enter bootloader or more like authentication e.g. with TA involvement? \n\n\u003e We only need this for development, right? Maybe it\u0027s something that we only enable in local builds, but not in production builds.\n\nThat is a problematic question. If we don\u0027t have that in mp builds, we just resign from the `flash_fp_mcu` script functionality, because there is no other method to force bootloader. Anyway, this CL adds possibility to include such command, guarded by the config.",
      "parentUuid": "1d6f6284_ebca4c7d",
      "revId": "ddb659b77b509f1784072da1a6becec4390e2789",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4db95822_5b034170",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-20T20:31:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e not to accidentally enter bootloader or more like authentication e.g. with TA involvement?\n\nI was thinking about something that would prevent an attacker with root access from being able to send the \"enter bootloader\" command to the FPMCU. I think it would need to involve authentication with TA, but I haven\u0027t thought it through. IIRC, GSC has some protocol for enabling some development features. Maybe we could re-use that?\n\n@lziest@google.com, what are your thoughts? We don\u0027t have access to the bootloader code, so it\u0027s hard to audit.\n\n\u003e  we just resign from the flash_fp_mcu script functionality, because there is no other method to force bootloader\n\nIs there any restriction on entering the bootloader when we\u0027re in RW? If we can limit the command to only the RW image, then that gives us the ability to turn the command off in RW if there are some security issues.",
      "parentUuid": "0302e8be_59385c6a",
      "revId": "ddb659b77b509f1784072da1a6becec4390e2789",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
